---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { getMeta } from '../utils/data';
const meta = getMeta();
const categories = [
  { label: 'Ordinary contact fouls', rate: 4 },
  { label: 'Off-ball monitoring', rate: 10 },
  { label: 'Traveling & out-of-bounds', rate: 16 },
  { label: 'Defensive 3s & shot clock', rate: 20 },
];
---

<Base
  title="What types of calls do refs miss?"
  current="attention-load"
  description="What types of calls do NBA refs miss, according to the Last Two Minute report data?"
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container prose">
      <h1 class="display">What types of calls do refs miss?</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        Using the NBA's Last Two Minute report — the league's public accounting of missed and incorrect calls in
        clutch time.
      </p>

      <h2>The question</h2>
      <p>
        What types of calls do refs miss? Are errors spread evenly across call types, or do certain situations
        produce more mistakes?
      </p>

      <h2>What we found</h2>
      <p>
        Errors are not uniform. Across 51,130 Last Two Minute events, miss rates vary sharply by call category.
        Ordinary contact fouls are missed least often. Traveling, out-of-bounds, defensive three-seconds, and
        off-ball monitoring situations are missed far more often — up to roughly <strong>{meta.headlines.attention_load_lift}×</strong> the
        baseline error rate in the highest-risk contexts.
      </p>

      <div class="chart-bars">
        {categories.map((c) => (
          <div class="chart-bar-row">
            <span>{c.label}</span>
            <div class="chart-bar-track"><div class="chart-bar-fill" style={`width:${c.rate * 5}%`}></div></div>
            <span class="mono">~{c.rate}%</span>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>

      <h2>Holdout seasons</h2>
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th>Season</th><th>Baseline error rate</th><th>Top 10% risk contexts</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>2021-22</td><td>7.7%</td><td>3.45× baseline</td></tr>
          <tr><td>2022-23</td><td>6.2%</td><td>3.93× baseline</td></tr>
          <tr><td>2023-24</td><td>6.0%</td><td>3.92× baseline</td></tr>
          <tr><td>2024-25</td><td>4.5%</td><td>4.00× baseline</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>

      <h2>What this means</h2>
      <p>
        Refs don't miss calls at random. The hardest situations to officiate — multiple moving parts, off-ball
        action, judgment calls on traveling and defensive positioning — are where errors concentrate. That's
        useful context for replay review, crew training, and understanding why certain late-game calls feel
        inconsistent.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
